  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Factory Vetting -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">What to Look for in Bangladesh Factory Vetting</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Vetting Bangladesh factories requires systematic verification of capabilities, compliance, and reliability. Whether working through agents or directly, due diligence is essential. This checklist covers key verification steps to ensure you partner with reputable manufacturers.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">BGMEA Membership Verification</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Verify factory membership in the Bangladesh Garment Manufacturers and Exporters Association (BGMEA) or Bangladesh Knitwear Manufacturers and Exporters Association (BKMEA). Membership indicates basic regulatory compliance and industry standing. Check the official BGMEA website factory directory to confirm membership status. Note that membership alone doesn't guarantee quality - it's a baseline requirement. SDF Clothing is a registered BGMEA member in good standing since 1998.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Third-Party Audit Reports</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Request recent audit reports from recognized third-party organizations including BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative), SEDEX (Supplier Ethical Data Exchange), WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production), and client-commissioned audits. These reports reveal working conditions, safety standards, and compliance issues. Verify audit authenticity with the issuing organization - certificates can be forged. SDF undergoes regular third-party audits and shares reports with qualified clients. Learn about our <a href="/certifications">complete certification portfolio</a>.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Certification Verification</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Verify sustainability and quality certifications directly with issuing bodies. Key certifications include GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) for organic cotton, OEKO-TEX Standard 100 for chemical safety, ISO 9001 for quality management, and C-TPAT for supply chain security. Check certificate validity on the issuing organization's website. SDF holds 13 international certifications covering quality, social compliance, and environmental standards. All certificates are verifiable through issuing organizations.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Factory Capacity vs Order Size</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Assess whether factory capacity matches your order volume and timeline. Ask about monthly production capacity, current utilization, and lead times. A factory at 100% capacity may delay your order or compromise quality. Conversely, a factory too large for your order may deprioritize your business. SDF has 75,000 sq ft of production space with capacity for 50,000+ pieces monthly, ensuring we can scale with your brand's growth while maintaining attention to smaller orders. We serve <a href="/clothing-manufacturers-for-startups">clothing manufacturers for startups</a> with flexible capacity.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Financial Stability Indicators</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Evaluate factory financial stability to ensure long-term reliability. Indicators include years in operation, ownership stability, investment in equipment and facilities, and client retention rates. Factories with frequent ownership changes or financial distress pose supply chain risk. SDF has operated continuously since 1998 under stable ownership, with consistent investment in equipment and facilities. Our client retention rate exceeds 85%, reflecting long-term relationships built on reliability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 8: FAQ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Sourcing Agent Service FAQ</h2>
      
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What does a clothing sourcing agent cost?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Clothing sourcing agent costs typically range from 5-15% commission on factory prices, paid by either the brand or factory. Flat fee arrangements range from $2,000-10,000 per project. Retainer models cost $500-2,000 monthly. SDF operates as a direct factory partner with no agent commission, saving brands 5-15% on production costs. Direct factory relationships eliminate middleman markup while providing full transparency on pricing.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do I need a sourcing agent to manufacture in Bangladesh?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            You do not need a sourcing agent to manufacture in Bangladesh. You can work directly with factories like SDF Clothing. Direct factory relationships offer lower costs, better communication, and greater transparency. Sourcing agents add value primarily for brands lacking time or expertise to vet factories. However, working directly with a reputable factory like SDF provides the same services - factory vetting, sampling, production management, QC - without the 5-15% agent commission.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the difference between a sourcing agent and a buying house?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            A sourcing agent typically works independently, connecting brands to factories for commission. A buying house is a larger organization with in-house teams handling design, sourcing, and production. Both charge commission or markup. SDF differs from both as a direct factory partner - we are the manufacturer, not an intermediary. We provide end-to-end production services without middleman costs, offering the same capabilities as buying houses at factory-direct pricing.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How do I know if a sourcing agent is trustworthy?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Verify a sourcing agent's trustworthiness by checking client references, requesting factory audit reports, confirming their physical presence in the manufacturing country, and reviewing their commission structure. Red flags include demanding upfront fees, refusing to disclose commission percentages, or working with only one or two factories. Trustworthy agents provide transparency, references, and access to multiple verified factories. SDF operates transparently as a direct factory with verifiable certifications and client references.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can SDF act as my sourcing agent in Bangladesh?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            SDF operates as a direct factory partner rather than a traditional sourcing agent. We provide all sourcing services - factory capability assessment, sampling, production management, quality control, and export documentation - but as the manufacturer, not a middleman. This model eliminates agent commission while providing comprehensive support. For brands needing production outside our core capabilities, we can coordinate with our partner network, still at direct factory pricing.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What documents should a sourcing agent provide?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            A professional sourcing agent should provide factory audit reports, certification verification (GOTS, OEKO-TEX, BSCI, WRAP), detailed cost breakdowns, production schedules, quality inspection reports, and export documentation. They should also provide a formal contract outlining services, fees, and responsibilities. SDF provides all documentation directly as the factory, including audit reports, certification certificates, detailed costing, and comprehensive production tracking.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does factory sourcing take in Bangladesh?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Factory sourcing in Bangladesh typically takes 1-3 weeks for initial identification and 2-4 weeks for sample development and approval. Total timeline from initial inquiry to production start is usually 4-7 weeks. SDF accelerates this process by providing immediate capability assessment and in-house sampling, reducing sourcing time to 2-3 weeks. Direct factory relationships eliminate the back-and-forth communication delays common with agent-mediated sourcing.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the risk of using a sourcing agent I find online?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Online sourcing agents pose several risks: hidden commission structures pushing specific factories, lack of physical presence in manufacturing countries, inability to verify factory conditions, potential for scams requiring upfront fees, and communication delays. Red flags include demanding payment before showing factories, refusing to provide references, or using only WhatsApp without formal contracts. Work with verified, established partners like SDF with physical factories and transparent operations. Learn more about <a href="/insights/avoiding-clothing-manufacturer-scams">avoiding clothing manufacturer scams</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
